 her baby and they let out  coos of admiration when Dumbo shows  himself for the first time  despite looking like a regular elephant  first Dumbo soon sneezes and what's his  gigantic ears run free  this causes the other elephants to laugh  and make jokes about mrs. Jumbo's new  baby causing her to lash out in anger  soon her companions give Dumbo his  unfortunate name and rudely laughs and  mrs. jumbo space which makes her even  more furious than before when it comes  to the live-action remake however the  storks are left in the past instead we  watch as Holt finds out that the circus  owner Maxima DC has sold his horses to  make ends meet after facing some  travelling times  this leaves Holt without an act luckily  the circus owners soon explains that  he's acquired a pregnant elephants named  mrs. jumbo and that he wants the fires  to look after it soon the baby elephant  is born and the fires find out that he  has exceptionally large ears but unlike  the original Dumbo receives his name  from a highly despicable crowd no more  talking animals as many of you surely  remember Dumbo and the rest of the  circus animals are able to talk  throughout the original movie however  things are very different in the  live-action remake instead of primarily  focusing on the lives of zoo animals the  remake centers around the lives of  people so if you're expecting to see  Dumbo and mrs. jumbo converse and sing  in the live-action remake you're sorely  mistaken since the film doesn't include  talking animals Dumbo's best friend and  mentor Timothy Mouse isn't a prominent  character although he can easily be  spotted in the 2019 remake his  character's purpose is primarily  replaced by the fire family mrs. jumbo  who could forget the agonizing scene  that served to separate mrs. jumbo  from her adorable baby Dumbo this  heart-wrenching scene is one of the many  reasons Millennials don't want to watch  the live-action remake in the original  film mrs. jumbo is labeled as a mad  